{"title":"2002 AMC 12P Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 12P Problems\">2002 AMC 12P #13</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems\">2002 AMC 10P #24</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which there is a set of distinct positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/4122ea231386a3bb5605c0aa7f49a9a064e70ba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1, k_2, ... k_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> for which\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da913f9b8644e18078f96cf0ab0c4e928633633.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k^2_1 + k^2_2 + ... + k^2_n = 2002?\\]\" width=\"203\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/0/2107689d5f08b289c74760ffe4750343da4e3efd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }14 \\qquad \\text{(B) }15 \\qquad \\text{(C) }16 \\qquad \\text{(D) }17 \\qquad \\text{(E) }18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/a/4fa8246c2ce4db60c3ddbb592ef0c29b932a65c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2_1 + k^2_2 + ... + k^2_n = 2002 \\geq \\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"359\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/3/b7341545d5484c6c86ae46c3edc15cf1f772613c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/3/073ed284acd506ca80ff384a8fdf70dc1f95b82c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6} = \\frac{(17)(18)(35)}{6} = 1785 &lt; 2002$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"385\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00e99f468a9d0856717d34f8258350da274cb3ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/5/f954d94edbafd3685a989a73cbde78b9c296a1a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n+1)(2n+1)}{6} = 1785 + 18^2 = 2109 &gt; 2002$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"368\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/7/8e732b2f8a0033d155f60a7575d2b5807765fba2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leq 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Now we must show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/3/b7341545d5484c6c86ae46c3edc15cf1f772613c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" /> works. We replace some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> within the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/8327b6d26ca5ad932a9eedcf56f8f53ccdfca015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, ... 17\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> with an integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc8677172151fa061e6a82aac7b154be25bd32e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> to account for the amount under <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e470b7ce7a2f4d0c1ae064d2874ca377693897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2002$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/40544c7715e1d6e1a33f347d2b3c714afccd787c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2002-1785 = 217$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Essentially, this boils down to writing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/7/ed7ae5e3303cff9e948a61a941eb64957853bb21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$217$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> as a difference of squares. Assume there exist positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddc8677172151fa061e6a82aac7b154be25bd32e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/8/868f33b090b12e63348a440f021558954fe55c29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\leq 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"17\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/9/809307e7e5c7a4c3d9f208327f7b7e3b68732a0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 - b^2 = 217$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We can rewrite this as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/a/41a63e0f256871c17835163124069044d8017509.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)(a-b) = 217$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a8a07834d4ddb6e7ae4c62444a8d1d9688811bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$217 = 7 \\cdot 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"94\" height=\"14\" />, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/611a35ff7ed4b1490a38864e2824618079bfb3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b = 217$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2ea7581c87e299152333019e7f838260fcefbe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc25e2a22818fde119b57a8328f45288c7c7bdd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f4576e0edf392cecf87952cd89c88f1409f107e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />. We analyze each case separately.\n</p><p>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/1/611a35ff7ed4b1490a38864e2824618079bfb3be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b = 217$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2ea7581c87e299152333019e7f838260fcefbe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Solving this system of equations gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c94d6170e2bba73b411713a1aa4191112b480b4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 109$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/0/f405d43771d8a292285132a656702c4313df55e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f563859040bfb07ac1320b388ba815f04c5aa58e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$108 &gt; 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />, so this case does not yield a solution.\n</p><p>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc25e2a22818fde119b57a8328f45288c7c7bdd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f4576e0edf392cecf87952cd89c88f1409f107e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-b = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Solving this system of equations gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/5367b662a5a7a38fd8ba8ebc5b42c62219ca2ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a450ff18c9509e2f70ba9f036b8ca9aeb33d49c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. This satisfies all the requirements of the problem.\n</p><p>The list <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4ce76f0d705001e9868b166cb8d78b2a008aa061.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2 ... 11, 13, 14 ... 17, 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"17\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> terms whose sum of squares equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96e470b7ce7a2f4d0c1ae064d2874ca377693897.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2002$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/9/649c799fcbf65a8078ed47e0efc4470e9b57e084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> is impossible, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/d/ccd0702ff9183ef18b36b6feea68235b10836631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf{(D) }17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_12P_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P\">2002 AMC 10P</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b>